.TH EXIT 1 "OShell Built-in Commands"
.SH NAME
exit \- exit the shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B exit
[
.I exit_code
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B exit
command terminates the OShell and returns an exit status to the parent process.
.PP
If
.I exit_code
is provided, it must be a numeric value that will be returned as the exit status.
If no
.I exit_code
is provided, the exit status is 0 (success).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B exit_code
An optional numeric exit code. Must be an integer.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B exit
Exit with status 0.
.TP
.B exit 0
Exit with status 0 (success).
.TP
.B exit 1
Exit with status 1 (failure).
.TP
.B exit 42
Exit with status 42.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns the specified
.I exit_code
or 0 if none specified.
.SH ERRORS
If a non-numeric argument is provided, prints "An error has occurred" and returns 1.
If more than one argument is provided, prints "An error has occurred" and returns 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1)